{%- if marked_verified %}
These rules are marked as expected failures but VERIFIED: {{ marked_verified | join(", ") }}. Either the defect is not
there, or the rule does not test for it. This draft cannot be stamped until that is resolved: fix the rule, or withdraw
the marking with expect_rule_passage.
{% endif %}
{%- if incomplete %}
These rules stopped on an assertion the prover generated rather than one of yours, so they never reached their property:
{% for rule in incomplete %}  {{ rule.name }}{% if rule.assertion %}: {{ rule.assertion }}{% endif %}
{% endfor -%}
None of these says whether the rule's property holds.
{%- for kind in advised %}
{%- if kind == "loopUnwinding" %}
A loop needed more iterations than the bound unrolls. Constrain what determines the trip count, or raise the bound. A
summary directive cannot name a loop. If the property is about the loop, skip it and say what bound it needed.
{%- elif kind == "cannotOverflow" %}
`Cannot overflow` is a check the Prover adds on its own, not one your rule asserts: it could not show that an expression
it treats as a pointer stays below 2^64. That is almost always because a value the rule reads from an account (a
balance, an amount) is free to sit just below u64::MAX. Bound the account-data values on that rule's path —
`cvlr_assume!(x < 1 << 63)` is enough — and record each bound as an assumption. A property about the top of the range
cannot take the bound: skip it and say so.
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
expect_rule_failure does not account for one of these: a marking claims a real defect, and none has been shown.
{% endif %}
{%- if unverdicted %}
No verdict came back for: {{ unverdicted | join(", ") }}. The prover's report does not name them, so they have not been
checked, and this draft cannot be stamped until they are. Run verify_rules again; if they are still missing, the run's
link is where to look.
{% endif %}
{%- if property_failures %}
Not accounted for: {{ property_failures | join(", ") }}. Fix the rule, or mark it with expect_rule_failure and say why
the failure is real.
{% endif %}
{%- if unfinished %}
{{ unfinished | join(", ") }} did not reach a property verdict. A timeout, an error, a sanity failure, or a skip is not a
finding, and expect_rule_failure does not account for one.
{% endif %}
{%- if stamped %}
Every rule is accounted for. This draft is stamped.
{% endif %}
